verage `f(x)/x`; the three can express the same underlying function and are inter-convertible given `initial_input`. The `TIME_SERIES_*` variants are the time-varying equivalents. Which form to use follows the data source: bid stacks are incremental, total cost tables input-output, efficiency tables average rate.\",\"discriminator\":{\"mapping\":{\"AVERAGE_RATE\":\"#/components/schemas/AverageRateCurve\",\"INCREMENTAL\":\"#/components/schemas/IncrementalCurve\",\"INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_AVERAGE_RATE\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INCREMENTAL\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\",\"TIME_SERIES_INPUT_OUTPUT\":\"#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},\"propertyName\":\"curve_type\"},\"oneOf\":[{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/InputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/IncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/AverageRateCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesInputOutputCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesIncrementalCurve\"},{\"\$ref\":\"https://openapi.invalid/schema/root-af9d0b5f8a5342306720.json#/components/schemas/TimeSeriesAverageRateCurve\"}],\"title\":\"ValueCurve\",\"type\":\"object\"},\"XY_Coords\":{\"description\":\"A single point, given as its `x` and `y` coordinates.\",\"properties\":{\"x\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"y\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"x\",\"y\"],\"title\":\"XY_Coords\",\"type\":\"object\"}}},\"info\":{\"description\":\"Power system investments models: Technologies, Financials, Requirements, SupplementalAttributes, and Portfolio components\",\"title\":\"PowerInvestmentsOpenA